From: Peter Lemenkov <lemenkov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Test the built hex_tarball in peer nodes

peer_call/4 appends the directory of the hex_tarball under test to the
code path of the peer node with code:add_path/1. If another hex_core
is already in the code path, e.g. installed system-wide in
/usr/share/erlang/lib, the peer loads that one instead, so
latin1_filename_encoding_test and printable_range_test test the wrong
code. Prepend the directory with code:add_patha/1.

Signed-off-by: Peter Lemenkov <lemenkov@gmail.com>
---
--- a/test/hex_tarball_SUITE.erl
+++ b/test/hex_tarball_SUITE.erl
@@ -2150,7 +2150,7 @@
             {ok, Pid, _Node} -> Pid
         end,
     try
-        true = peer:call(Peer, code, add_path, [filename:dirname(code:which(hex_tarball))]),
+        true = peer:call(Peer, code, add_patha, [filename:dirname(code:which(hex_tarball))]),
         peer:call(Peer, Module, Function, Arguments, 30000)
     after
         peer:stop(Peer)
